        "text": "[stamped mark] 18128",
        "@annotation": {
         "@id": "copies/yk645sm6970#transcription-annotation",
         "belief": {
          "@type": "belief",
          "@id": "copies/yk645sm6970#transcription-belief",
          "certainty": "likely",
          "reasons": [
           {
            "@type": "meaningComprehension",
            "comprehends": [
             "copies/yk645sm6970#inscription"
            ],
            "note": "Graded medium on the figures of the date: one figure is arguable. Stamped, running down the roll at about sixty degrees, upright in the lower panel after rotation. A heavily inked mark, a vertical with two bars projecting to the right and a detached blob below it, stands before five plain figures, 1 8 1 2 8. The same mark, down to the detached blob, precedes the figures on rd899zb5188 and jd143sb1087 in batch 32, and on none of the three can it be read as a figure without destroying the date, so I take it for a fixed slug rather than a digit. Five figures with the leading zeros dropped give 18.1.28. Later than the 1904-1926 span reading.md reports, as is md908xy8241."
           }
          ]
         }
        }
       }
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
   "scan": "https://stacks.stanford.edu/image/iiif/yk645sm6970%2Fyk645sm6970_0001/",
